    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363-a1">

                <pb facs="0690" n="1344" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1344"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 319.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Cherif Pasha to Mr.
                            Beardsley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1875-05-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 22,
                    1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Agent and Consul-General</hi>: Referring to my
                    circular-dispatch of the 18th instant, I have the honor to inform you that the
                    government of the Khedive, following the measures already taken, has decided
                    that the installation of the court; of appeals and that of the tribunal of first
                    instance will take place at Alexandria on the 28th of June next, and that their
                    functioning, in conformity with the 38th article of the judiciary organization,
                    will begin with the 18th day of October following. It will, therefore, be
                    beginning with October 18, 1875, that the laws which compose the new Egyptian
                    code and which the government will promulgate within the time and in the manner
                    prescribed by the 35th Article of said regulations, will become binding through
                    the whole territory of the country.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, Mr. Agent and Consul-General, the assurances of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>CHERIF.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
